Replace herdr's generated worktree/branch word list (adjective + noun, e.g.
"brave-river") with a single word list of hololive talent nicknames (JP/EN/ID
branches + graduated members), e.g. "okayu". Source list fetched from
https://hololive.hololivepro.com/talents on 2026-09-19.

This is a personal-taste patch, not a behavior fix. The upstream feature
request asking for the word list to become configurable instead of hardcoded,
https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr/issues/4374 (filed 2026-09-19), was closed
as not planned on 2026-09-19 — herdr's `[worktrees]` config only exposes
`directory` (no word-list key), so there is no config-driven exit either.

This is now a **permanent local patch** (decided in tarotene/dotfiles#449,
2026-09-25): the not-planned closure means there is no upstream path to drop
it on, and the word list backs the herdr sidebar's `$oshi` fan-mark feature
(`config/herdr/oshi-marks.tsv`, the CI cross-check in `.github/workflows/
ci.yml`, and the metadata hooks under `config/{claude,codex,copilot}/hooks/`)
— removing the patch would remove that feature, not just revert cosmetic
naming. When a `nixpkgs-unstable` bump shifts `src/worktree.rs` enough that
this patch stops applying, re-fit it against the new source: re-diff
`generated_branch_slug` and its test
`generated_branch_slug_is_worktree_namespaced_and_stable` from the new
upstream tree, keeping the same hololive-nickname word list.

